            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0449" n="443" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg443"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851R.01/12¼</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State (Welles) to the Chief of Staff, United States Army (Marshall)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-17">November 17,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General Marshall</hi>: I am entirely in
                    accord with the suggestions contained in the last paragraph of your letter to me
                    of November 16. I shall consequently be grateful if you will convey to General
                    Eisenhower the sense of the desires of the President and if you will be kind
                    enough to let us know here in the Department of State when a reply is
                    received.</p>
                <p>Believe me</p>
                <p>Yours very sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
